course: dictionary
lesson: 15964
title: Untrustworthy
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Untrustworthy means not able to be trusted. You cannot rely on it to tell the truth or keep its promises. «The man lied about the price, so we think he is untrustworthy.»
explain: Break the word into parts. Un- means not, trust means believing someone will be honest, and -worthy means deserving. So an untrustworthy person or thing does not deserve your trust. Check the context: does someone lie, break promises, or give information that may be false?
explain: Untrustworthy can describe people or information. «The message promised free prizes, but it asked for my password, so it looked untrustworthy.» Online, fake websites and scam messages are untrustworthy, so do not believe them without checking.
fact: Untrustworthy means not able to be trusted.
fact: Untrustworthy is an adjective: untrustworthy, more untrustworthy, most untrustworthy.
fact: Un- at the start means not, so untrustworthy is the opposite of trustworthy.
fact: «An untrustworthy source» may contain false information, so check it with another source.
fact: Useful phrases: «an untrustworthy person» and «look untrustworthy».
exercise: «The shopkeeper hid the broken vase and lied about it. He is untrustworthy.» What does untrustworthy mean? | Very funny and kind | Good at painting | *Not able to be trusted | Able to fly
exercise: «The email said I had won a prize, but it looked untrustworthy.» Which word means the opposite of untrustworthy? | Careless | *Trustworthy | Loud | Funny
exercise: Which is the best reason to call a website untrustworthy? | It has bright pictures of cats | It is written in short sentences | *It asks for your password and may be a scam | It is very old
test: «My friend always broke her promises, so Sam now thinks she is untrustworthy.» What does untrustworthy mean here? | Kind and generous | Very tall | Good at football | *Cannot be relied on to keep promises
test: Which sentence uses untrustworthy correctly? | I went to the untrustworthy park to play. | *The untrustworthy man sold me fake tickets. | The untrustworthy sun shone brightly. | The untrustworthy cake was baked by my nan.
exam: A news site often posts false stories and asks for your bank details. What does this tell you? | The site is trustworthy | The site is brand new and clean | The site is very friendly | *The site is untrustworthy
